            and the findings.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- DIFFERENT -->
    <section style="padding-top:0">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">What makes this different</div>
        <h2>Most tools show you numbers. We tell you what to do about them.</h2>

        <div class="diffs">
          <div class="diff">
            <h3>A person actually reads your account</h3>
            <p>
              Not an alert. Not a chatbot. Someone looks at your store every month, writes the
              recommendations, and puts their name on them.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="diff">
            <h3>We tell you when nothing needs changing</h3>
            <p>
              Some months are fine. We say so instead of inventing three problems. That's why you'll
              believe us on the months we don't.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="diff">
            <h3>Read-only, and no customer data</h3>
            <p>
              We never write to your store or touch your campaigns. We don't collect your customers'
              names, emails or addresses at all — we don't need them.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="diff">
            <h3>Every calculation is published</h3>
            <p>
              What we mean by "net sales", "new customer" or "profit" is written down on one page you
              can read. It doesn't change quietly.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="diff">
            <h3>Checked against your own tools first</h3>
            <p>
              Before a report goes out, our totals are compared to what Shopify and your ad platforms
              show. Where there's a difference, we explain it in the report.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="diff">
            <h3>Priced on ad spend, not your sales</h3>
            <p>
              Most tools charge more as your revenue grows, whether or not you use them more. Ours
              doesn't. Grow all you like — the price stays put.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

